Debian's packaging on upstream after 4.3.31.

- Upstream takes the directory for pidfiles and sockets from XYMONRUNDIR
  and XYMONCLIENTRUNDIR at configure time, where 4.3.31 had it in each
  command line. Debian's 12_hobbitvars.patch pointed those command lines
  at /var/run/xymon; set the two variables to the same place instead.
- The client's tmp and log directories. Debian's 12_hobbitvars.patch wrote
  them into xymonclient.cfg as XYMONTMP and XYMONCLIENTLOGS. Upstream now
  takes them at configure time, INSTALLCLIENTTMPDIR and INSTALLCLIENTLOGDIR
  (xymon#411), and links each from the client's home itself: so Debian's
  two rmdir find a link, and remove whichever is there before making
  Debian's own link.
  What the file says depends on the tree. With xymon#906 it names the two
  directories by reference and the programs hold them, from those same two
  variables: nothing to do. Without it, and in a preview made before it,
  the two lines are set on the installed file to the values Debian's patch
  gave them; a patch cannot, as main and the previews write those lines
  differently. The greps fail the build if the lines are neither.
  When every tree built has xymon#906, the else branch can go.
- Upstream has a second page in man7, xymon-tls.7. Debian's rules move
  xymon.7 to the client package and remove the directory, which was then
  empty: remove it only when it is. xymon-tls.7 stays in the server
  package.

Goes when Debian packages a version that has these.

--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -28,6 +28,10 @@
 	SECUREXYMONCGIURL=/xymon-seccgi \
 	HTTPDGID=www-data \
 	XYMONLOGDIR=/var/log/xymon \
+	XYMONRUNDIR=/var/run/xymon \
+	XYMONCLIENTRUNDIR=/var/run/xymon \
+	INSTALLCLIENTTMPDIR=/var/lib/xymon/tmp \
+	INSTALLCLIENTLOGDIR=/var/log/xymon \
 	XYMONHOSTNAME=localhost \
 	XYMONHOSTIP=127.0.0.1 \
 	MANROOT=/usr/share/man \
@@ -86,8 +90,19 @@
 # CLIENT
 	CFLAGS="$(CFLAGS) $(CPPFLAGS) $(LDFLAGS)" PKGBUILD=1 INSTALLROOT=$C/ $(MAKE) install-client
 	cd $C/usr/lib/xymon/client && mv etc/* $C/etc/xymon && rmdir etc && ln -s ../../../../etc/xymon etc
-	cd $C/usr/lib/xymon/client && rmdir logs && ln -s ../../../../var/log/xymon logs
-	cd $C/usr/lib/xymon/client && rmdir tmp && ln -s ../../../../var/lib/xymon/tmp
+	cd $C/usr/lib/xymon/client && { rm -f logs 2>/dev/null || rmdir logs; } && ln -s ../../../../var/log/xymon logs
+	cd $C/usr/lib/xymon/client && { rm -f tmp 2>/dev/null || rmdir tmp; } && ln -s ../../../../var/lib/xymon/tmp
+	# XYMONTMP and XYMONCLIENTLOGS in xymonclient.cfg, see debian/patches/12_hobbitvars.patch
+	if grep -q '^XYMONTMP="\$$XYMONCLIENTTMPDIR"' $C/etc/xymon/xymonclient.cfg && \
+	   grep -q '^XYMONCLIENTLOGS="\$$XYMONCLIENTLOGDIR"' $C/etc/xymon/xymonclient.cfg; then \
+		echo 'xymonclient.cfg names the tmp and log directories by reference: the programs hold them'; \
+	else \
+		sed -i -e 's|^XYMONTMP=.*|XYMONTMP="/var/lib/xymon/tmp"     # Where we may store temporary files.|' \
+			-e 's|^XYMONCLIENTLOGS=.*|XYMONCLIENTLOGS="/var/log/xymon"  # Where we store the client logfiles|' \
+			$C/etc/xymon/xymonclient.cfg && \
+		grep -q '^XYMONTMP="/var/lib/xymon/tmp"' $C/etc/xymon/xymonclient.cfg && \
+		grep -q '^XYMONCLIENTLOGS="/var/log/xymon"' $C/etc/xymon/xymonclient.cfg; \
+	fi
 	# the only command needed in /usr/bin is xymoncmd, its PATH includes our private .../bin
 	cd $C/usr/bin && ln -s ../lib/xymon/client/bin/xymoncmd xymoncmd
 	cp debian/xymon-client.default.template $C/usr/share/xymon/xymon-client.default.template
@@ -99,7 +114,7 @@
 				rm -v $$f ; ln -s ../../client/bin/$$f ; \
 			fi \
 		done
-	rmdir $S/usr/share/man/man7
+	rmdir --ignore-fail-on-non-empty $S/usr/share/man/man7
 
 	# move xymond_client to xymon-client package (see #903614):
 	mv $S/usr/share/man/man8/xymond_client.8 $C/usr/share/man/man8/
